From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:00:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: panorama scroll trace in the crash log dump
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Users report that a panorama shelf sometimes stops dead after a swipe,
away from the edges. Reading the code does not tell which path ends the
fling, so the grid now logs what happened, and "Dump crash logs"
appends the last 400 events.

Per touch it logs down and up. Up carries the move count, the gap between
the last move and the release, the velocity from Compose's tracker, and
the velocity of the last 100 ms of samples. Compose reports 0 when that
gap is over 40 ms, so a stalled touch stream shows trackerV=0 next to a
non-zero recentV.

Per fling it logs the start velocity, then how it ended: done, stopped
(remaining velocity), or cancelled. It also logs any frame that consumed
less than it asked for, and the longest frame gap. scrollToItem,
requestScrollToItem and scrollToOffset log themselves, so a cancel is
preceded by its cause. A measure that moves the offset logs its reason
(request, restore, anchor, clamp), as do epoch changes and changes to the
scroll range mid-scroll. Grid enter/leave and userScrollEnabled=false
are logged too.

Release builds are minified, so every entry point writes its own label
instead of a stack trace. Scrolling is unchanged. The fling wrapper
forwards every delta, and the touch observer reads the Initial pass
without consuming anything.

